{
  "name": "Wall of Cutting Light",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "modules/titan-vttrpg-compendium/icons/traditions/Light_Tradition_Icon.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p>You create a wall formed by criss-crossing beams of concentrated light to burn any who pass through.</p><p>Draw a <strong>line</strong> up to <strong>10 spaces long</strong>, or a <strong>circle</strong> with a <strong>radius</strong> between <strong>1-2 spaces</strong>. Each space must be within <strong>30 spaces</strong> of you.</p><p>A wall of light appears in the selected area. This wall <strong>is 2 spaces high</strong> and lasts until the start of your next turn.</p><p>When you cast this spell, each creature within the affected area may make an opposed <strong>Reflexes</strong> check to immediately move to either side of the wall.</p><p>Any creature that enters the wall or starts its turn there takes <strong>1 Damage</strong>, which ignores <strong>Armor</strong>.</p><p>Each extra success extends the duration of the wall by <strong>+1 rounds</strong>.</p><p>Alternatively, you can increase the <strong>Damage</strong> by <strong>+1</strong> per extra success.</p>",
